@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `br-interpretation-time`

-- Decreto-Lei 4.657/1942 (LINDB), arts. 2 to 6: how long a law lasts, what a later law does to an earlier one,
-- whether a repealed law comes back, and what a law in force leaves alone.
-- The days a law begins and ceases to bind come from br-interpretation-time.l4; this module takes them as inputs.
-- Whatever the text does not answer is a named REFUSE: which of art. 2 par. 1 and par. 2 prevails when both apply,
-- when a temporary law ceases, what a re-enactment does, and a right that sits on both readings of art. 6 par. 2.

§ `LINDB arts. 2 to 6: the life of a law`

§§ `Art. 2: how long a law lasts, and when a later law revokes an earlier one`

-- src:16 | Art. 2o Não se destinando à vigência temporária, a lei terá vigor até que outra a modifique ou revogue.
-- src:17 | § 1o A lei posterior revoga a anterior quando expressamente o declare, quando seja com ela incompatível ou quando regule inteiramente a matéria de que tratava a lei anterior.
-- src:18 | § 2o A lei nova, que estabeleça disposições gerais ou especiais a par das já existentes, não revoga nem modifica a lei anterior.
-- src:19 | § 3o Salvo disposição em contrário, a lei revogada não se restaura por ter a lei revogadora perdido a vigência.
@ref LINDB art. 2 caput to par. 3 (src:16-19)
DECLARE `A law as art. 2 caput sees it` HAS
    `it was not meant for temporary operation`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day it begins to bind`                                           IS A DATE
    `the day a later law that modifies or revokes it begins to bind`      IS A MAYBE DATE

@ref LINDB art. 2 par. 1 and par. 2 (src:17-18)
DECLARE `How a later law stands to an earlier one` HAS
    `it is later than the earlier law`                                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `it expressly declares the earlier law revoked`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is incompatible with the earlier law`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it regulates entirely the matter the earlier law regulated`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `it establishes general or special provisions alongside those already existing`                    IS A BOOLEAN

@ref LINDB art. 2 par. 1 and par. 2 (src:17-18)
DECLARE `What art. 2 says happens to the earlier law` IS ONE OF
    `the earlier law is revoked`
    `the earlier law is neither revoked nor modified`
    `art. 2 lists no ground for revoking the earlier law`

@ref LINDB art. 2 caput (src:16)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not say when a temporary law ceases` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 2 caput speaks only of a law not meant for temporary operation, and the text does not say when a temporary law ceases"

-- "Nao se destinando a vigencia temporaria, a lei tera vigor ate que outra a modifique ou revogue."
-- A law not meant to be temporary stays in force from the day it begins to bind until a later law modifies or revokes it.
-- On the two boundary days the answer turns on a moment of the day that the text does not give (art. 1), so they are refused.
@ref LINDB art. 2 caput (src:16)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      law IS A `A law as art. 2 caput sees it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the law is in force on` d `, as art. 2 caput has it` law MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF d LESS THAN law's `the day it begins to bind` THEN FALSE
        IF d EQUALS law's `the day it begins to bind` THEN `the text gives no moment of the day`
        IF NOT law's `it was not meant for temporary operation` THEN `the text does not say when a temporary law ceases`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER law's `the day a later law that modifies or revokes it begins to bind`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST r THEN
                BRANCH
                    IF d LESS THAN r THEN TRUE
                    IF d EQUALS r THEN `the text gives no moment of the day`
                    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "A lei posterior revoga a anterior quando expressamente o declare, quando seja com ela incompativel ou quando regule inteiramente a materia ..."
-- Read as sufficient grounds and, with art. 2 caput (a law lasts until another modifies or revokes it), as the grounds there are:
-- a later law revokes the earlier one on one of these three, and on no other ground art. 2 lists.
@ref LINDB art. 2 par. 1 (src:17)
GIVEN r IS A `How a later law stands to an earlier one`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a ground listed in art. 2 par. 1 exists` r MEANS
        r's `it is later than the earlier law`
    AND (   r's `it expressly declares the earlier law revoked`
         OR r's `it is incompatible with the earlier law`
         OR r's `it regulates entirely the matter the earlier law regulated`)

@ref LINDB art. 2 par. 1 and par. 2 (src:17-18)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not say which of par. 1 and par. 2 prevails` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 2 par. 2 says a new law alongside the existing provisions neither revokes nor modifies, par. 1 lists grounds on which a later law revokes, and the text does not say which prevails when both apply"

-- Par. 2: a new law that sets provisions alongside those already existing neither revokes nor modifies the earlier law.
-- When a par. 1 ground is also present the text does not say which of the two paragraphs prevails.
@ref LINDB art. 2 par. 1 and par. 2 (src:17-18)
GIVEN r IS A `How a later law stands to an earlier one`
GIVETH A `What art. 2 says happens to the earlier law`
`what art. 2 par. 1 and par. 2 say happens to the earlier law` r MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT r's `it is later than the earlier law` THEN `art. 2 lists no ground for revoking the earlier law`
        IF `a ground listed in art. 2 par. 1 exists` r
           AND r's `it establishes general or special provisions alongside those already existing`
        THEN `the text does not say which of par. 1 and par. 2 prevails`
        IF `a ground listed in art. 2 par. 1 exists` r THEN `the earlier law is revoked`
        IF r's `it establishes general or special provisions alongside those already existing`
        THEN `the earlier law is neither revoked nor modified`
        OTHERWISE `art. 2 lists no ground for revoking the earlier law`

-- Par. 3: "Salvo disposicao em contrario, a lei revogada nao se restaura por ter a lei revogadora perdido a vigencia."
-- Whose provision counts as "contrario" is not said, so the caller says whether one exists, from wherever it comes.
@ref LINDB art. 2 par. 3 (src:19)
GIVEN `a provision to the contrary restores the revoked law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a revoked law is restored when the revoking law loses force` `a provision to the contrary restores the revoked law` MEANS
    `a provision to the contrary restores the revoked law`

-- Nothing in the text says what a re-enactment does to what was done under the text it re-enacts.
@ref LINDB (no provision on repeal and re-enactment)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text has no rule on repeal and re-enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text has no rule on what a re-enactment does to what was done under the text it re-enacts"

@ref LINDB (no provision on repeal and re-enactment)
GIVEN `the day the old text was repealed` IS A DATE
      `the day the text was re-enacted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`what was done under a repealed text stands after its re-enactment` `the day the old text was repealed` `the day the text was re-enacted` MEANS
    `the text has no rule on repeal and re-enactment`

§§ `Art. 3: ignorance of the law`

-- src:20 | Art. 3o Ninguém se escusa de cumprir a lei, alegando que não a conhece.
@ref LINDB art. 3 (src:20)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`alleging that one does not know the law excuses compliance` MEANS FALSE

§§ `Art. 4: a case on which the law is silent`

-- src:21 | Art. 4o Quando a lei for omissa, o juiz decidirá o caso de acordo com a analogia, os costumes e os princípios gerais de direito.
@ref LINDB art. 4 (src:21)
DECLARE `Source a judge decides by when the law is silent` IS ONE OF
    analogy
    `custom`
    `general principles of law`

-- The three sources are listed in one breath, and the text does not rank them or say whether the judge needs all of them or any.
-- So the encoding lists them and answers only whether a source is among those art. 4 names.
@ref LINDB art. 4 (src:21)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Source a judge decides by when the law is silent`
`the sources art. 4 names for a case on which the law is silent` MEANS
    LIST analogy, `custom`, `general principles of law`

@ref LINDB art. 4 (src:21)
GIVEN source IS A `Source a judge decides by when the law is silent`
      `the law is silent on the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 4 names the source` source `for a case when the law is silent` `the law is silent on the case` MEANS
    IF `the law is silent on the case`
    THEN elem source `the sources art. 4 names for a case on which the law is silent`
    ELSE `art. 4 speaks only of a case on which the law is silent`

@ref LINDB art. 4 (src:21)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`art. 4 speaks only of a case on which the law is silent` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 4 speaks only of a case on which the law is silent and says nothing of the sources for any other case"

§§ `Art. 5: the ends the judge attends to`

-- src:22 | Art. 5o Na aplicação da lei, o juiz atenderá aos fins sociais a que ela se dirige e às exigências do bem comum.
@ref LINDB art. 5 (src:22)
DECLARE `How a judge applied the law` HAS
    `the judge attended to the social ends the law is directed at` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the judge attended to the demands of the common good`          IS A BOOLEAN

-- Art. 5 states what the judge attends to, not what the judge concludes. It is carried as a record of how the law was applied,
-- never as a computation of the right answer: whether the ends and the common good were in fact served is the judge's.
@ref LINDB art. 5 (src:22)
GIVEN how IS A `How a judge applied the law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the judge applied the law as art. 5 requires` how MEANS
        how's `the judge attended to the social ends the law is directed at`
    AND how's `the judge attended to the demands of the common good`

§§ `Art. 6: what a law in force leaves alone`

-- src:23 | Art. 6º A Lei em vigor terá efeito imediato e geral, respeitados o ato jurídico perfeito, o direito adquirido e a coisa julgada.
-- src:24 | § 1º Reputa-se ato jurídico perfeito o já consumado segundo a lei vigente ao tempo em que se efetuou.
-- src:25 | § 2º Consideram-se adquiridos assim os direitos que o seu titular, ou alguém por êle, possa exercer, como aquêles cujo comêço do exercício tenha têrmo pré-fixo, ou condição pré-estabelecida inalterável, a arbítrio de outrem.
-- src:26 | § 3º Chama-se coisa julgada ou caso julgado a decisão judicial de que já não caiba recurso.
@ref LINDB art. 6 caput to par. 3 (src:23-26)
DECLARE `A thing a law in force might reach` HAS
    `it is an act consummated under the law in force when it was done`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `its holder, or someone for the holder, can exercise the right`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the start of the exercise of the right has a term fixed beforehand`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the start of the exercise of the right has a condition established beforehand`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `that term or condition can be altered at the discretion of another person`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a judicial decision`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `an appeal still lies from it`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN

-- Par. 1: a perfect juridical act is one already consummated under the law in force when it was done.
@ref LINDB art. 6 par. 1 (src:24)
GIVEN x IS A `A thing a law in force might reach`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is a perfect juridical act` x MEANS
    x's `it is an act consummated under the law in force when it was done`

-- Par. 3: res judicata is a judicial decision from which no appeal lies any longer.
@ref LINDB art. 6 par. 3 (src:26)
GIVEN x IS A `A thing a law in force might reach`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is res judicata` x MEANS
        x's `it is a judicial decision`
    AND NOT x's `an appeal still lies from it`

@ref LINDB art. 6 par. 2 (src:25)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not say whether alterable at another's discretion qualifies a term` MEANS
    REFUSE "art. 6 par. 2 does not say whether 'inalteravel, a arbitrio de outrem' qualifies a term fixed beforehand as well as a condition established beforehand"

-- Par. 2: acquired rights are those the holder, or someone for the holder, can exercise, and those whose start of exercise has
-- a term fixed beforehand or a condition established beforehand that is unalterable at the discretion of another.
-- The words "inalteravel, a arbitrio de outrem" follow "condicao" and may or may not reach "termo" too (fork F-6): the two readings
-- differ only for a term fixed beforehand that another person can alter, which is refused.
@ref LINDB art. 6 par. 2 (src:25)
GIVEN x IS A `A thing a law in force might reach`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is an acquired right` x MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF x's `its holder, or someone for the holder, can exercise the right` THEN TRUE
        IF     x's `the start of the exercise of the right has a term fixed beforehand`
           AND x's `that term or condition can be altered at the discretion of another person`
        THEN `the text does not say whether alterable at another's discretion qualifies a term`
        IF x's `the start of the exercise of the right has a term fixed beforehand` THEN TRUE
        IF     x's `the start of the exercise of the right has a condition established beforehand`
           AND NOT x's `that term or condition can be altered at the discretion of another person`
        THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Caput: a law in force takes immediate and general effect, respecting the perfect juridical act, the acquired right and res judicata.
-- This is also what a repeal does to what was done under the repealed text: what the caput respects is left alone.
-- The three respects are tried in an order that lets a determinate one decide before the refusable one (acquired right) is reached.
@ref LINDB art. 6 caput (src:23)
GIVEN x IS A `A thing a law in force might reach`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art. 6 requires a law in force to respect it` x MEANS
        `it is a perfect juridical act` x
    OR  `it is res judicata` x
    OR  `it is an acquired right` x

@ref LINDB art. 6 caput (src:23)
GIVEN x IS A `A thing a law in force might reach`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a law in force takes immediate effect on` x MEANS
    NOT `art. 6 requires a law in force to respect it` x
